BT /F1 10 Tf 52 748 Td (BOOK COACH / DEMO GUIDE) Tj ET
BT /F1 18 Tf 52 712 Td (Worked example: daily cafe drink sales) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 52 674 Td (Question and scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 651 Td (How many drinks does one fictional cafe sell on a typical weekday? Count drinks, not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 635 Td (customers. Assume the cafe is open for eight hours. These numbers are invented for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 619 Td (demonstration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 52 580 Td (Drivers and assumptions) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 557 Td (Assume two busy hours at 120 drinks per hour and six quieter hours at 40 drinks per) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 541 Td (hour. The daily total is the busy-period sales plus the quieter-period sales.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 52 502 Td (Calculation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 479 Td (Busy period: 2 hours x 120 drinks/hour = 240 drinks. Quieter period: 6 hours x 40) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 463 Td (drinks/hour = 240 drinks. Total: 240 + 240 = 480 drinks per day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 52 424 Td (Plausibility and sensitivity) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 401 Td (Assume a capacity of 150 drinks per hour. The busy-hour estimate of 120 is below that) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 385 Td (capacity. If busy-hour sales range from 90 to 150, the daily estimate ranges from 420) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 369 Td (to 540 drinks, holding quieter sales fixed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 52 330 Td (What to validate) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 307 Td (Ask for point-of-sale counts by hour to check the assumed busy-hour sales rate. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 52 291 Td (example illustrates a reasoning process; it is not market research or a forecast.) Tj ET
